<https://seeds.local/item/sd-non.1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "a write that adds a blocker X is refused when X has its own blocker (create --deps AND dep add)" .
<https://seeds.local/item/sd-non.1> <https://seeds.local/ontology/childOf> <https://seeds.local/item/sd-non> .
<https://seeds.local/item/sd-non.1> <https://seeds.local/ontology/closeReason> "fixed in #6 (44bef05): validate_batch drops a target's edges to seeds that are not loaded; regression test a_blocker_that_has_its_own_blocker_can_be_added" .
<https://seeds.local/item/sd-non.1> <https://seeds.local/ontology/createdBy> "wu" .
<https://seeds.local/item/sd-non.1> <https://seeds.local/ontology/description> "Repro (2026-09-30, repo-local pendant): create A; create B --deps A; then 'create C --deps B' OR 'create C; dep add C B' -> rc=5 'B blockedOn: camayoc: blockedOn must point at a WorkItem the graph actually holds'. --dry-run passes. It succeeds only if C ALREADY depends on A (then A is in the validated subgraph). INFERRED: the write validates C plus its direct targets, whose blockedOn edges point at seeds outside that subgraph. Blocks any dependency chain deeper than 2." .
<https://seeds.local/item/sd-non.1> <https://seeds.local/ontology/issueType> "bug" .
<https://seeds.local/item/sd-non.1> <https://seeds.local/ontology/label> "dogfood" .
